reasoning_over_luck.evidence:
CHANCE. The only randomness is the setup order of the lots, which decides which seat sees which lots.

VARIANCE. The values a seat can keep range from four (2,3) lots, keeping 12, to four (1,4) lots, keeping 16. That is a 4-point swing out of about 60. Colour concentration and auction outcomes matter more.

WHEN ALL PLAY WELL. The winner is decided by:
- tracking announced auction cards, which narrow each kept card to one of two colours and accumulate across rounds;
- inferring rivals' hidden majorities;
- bid sizing against a simultaneous rival;
- using worth shifts to devalue a rival's colour.
The deal does not decide it alone.

INFERENCE. There is real hidden information (kept colours, holdings) with real levers to act on it: keep choice, bids, shifts, and bluffing talk.

ESTIMATE. Roughly 15-25% of the outcome is luck. A skilled player is clearly favoured over a thoughtless one.
